{
  "instrument": "planner_matrix",
  "command": "make run-devtool TOOL=planner_score_quality ARGS='--matrix --json'",
  "measured_on": "2026-11-09, the half-marathon moderate joins the offer (Alpha), its first readings with rulebook 6's half-marathon taper band (taper_volume_drop 0.40-0.60, the taper reviews; the plans read 0.43-0.52): running_half_marathon_moderate 0.0262 and _low 0.0262 (recovery_cadence 0.25: the 10-week plan has one easier week in nine, its load weeks 5-8 running into the taper; recovery_week_test_frequency 0.16: the 12-week plan tests in weeks 1 and 8, two of its three occasions, against 0.35-0.55), _high 0.0278 (the same, and taper_quality_share 0.025), _wide 0.0098 (recovery_cadence 0.11: the 8-week plan has one easier week in six; taper_quality_share 0.04 at 24 weeks). No other cell moved. 2026-11-08, the Ironman moderate joins the offer (Alpha), its first readings: ironman_moderate 0.0005 (race_day_freshness_ratio 0.018), ironman_moderate_low 0.0005 (first_long_session_fit 0.019: the ramp's step floor opens the long run a little above the low athlete's recent longest), ironman_moderate_high 0.0071 (first_week_fit 0.30: a 12-hour athlete's test week is the moderate tier's), ironman_moderate_wide 0.0032 (phase_share_base 0.13 at 36 weeks). Read lower after the week's planner merges (85ded1a): half_ironman_moderate_high 0.0040 -> 0.0030 (first_week_fit 0.21 -> 0.16), half_ironman_moderate_low 0.0004 -> 0.0002 (first_long_session_fit 0.019 -> 0.011). 2026-10-11, the fitness tests on a cadence (week 1, then every eight weeks; trail 20K BASIC opens with a test week whose Sunday is easy): trail_20k_basic_low 0.0000 -> 0.0015 (first_long_session_fit 0.0229: the long run now opens in week 2 at 59 from a 51-minute longest, the ramp's 10-minute step floor, where the squeezed week 1 had capped it at 52; the same reading the half_ironman_moderate_low cell carries). 2026-10-11, rulebook 6 and two card changes (sweet spot at 90 % FTP reads zone 3, hard swims warm up 500 m): half_ironman_moderate 0.0484 -> 0.0000, half_ironman_moderate_low 0.0484 -> 0.0004 (first_long_session_fit 0.02: the ramp's 10-minute step floor opens a 51-minute longest run at 59), half_ironman_moderate_high 0.0373 -> 0.0040 (first_week_fit 0.21: an 11.2 h athlete's test week is 7.2 h, the moderate tier's), trail_20k_basic_low 0.0099 -> 0.0000 (the taper may hold up to 1.5 times the peak week's sessions). 2026-10-10, the half-Ironman moderate joins the offer, its first readings: half_ironman_moderate 0.0484, half_ironman_moderate_low 0.0484 (the same plan: the tests are fixed-size and the easy sessions sit at their menu minimums), half_ironman_moderate_high 0.0373. Off band in all three: first_long_session_fit (1.0 for the default and low athlete: a 30-minute longest swim against the 1800 m pool floor, 0.24 for the high), hard_sessions_per_week 0.57 (the bench reads the sweet-spot long ride and the race-effort brick as zone 4, 4.6 hard sessions a week against 4), warmup_before_hard 0.44 (400 m swim warm-ups under the 10-minute line), taper_volume_drop 0.26 (the taper and race week average against a 13.5 h peak), recovery_week_test_frequency 0.13 (tests in the first week, the second base recovery week and one build recovery week, not every recovery week), monotony 0.08-0.09; the high athlete's first_week_fit 0.21 (an 11.2 h athlete's test week is 7.2 h). 2026-10-08, the _low family checks the plan's volume floor, 0.85 of the default (2.1 h/wk for the trail 20K basic; it was 0.75, below the floor): trail_20k_basic_low 0.0194 -> 0.0099. 2026-10-08, the review's open points: recovery slots 35-45 easy, 30-36 strides, long 45-60/45-75/60-80 by phase (a 4 h/wk athlete's recovery week reads 0.51-0.59, was 0.48), the base long run up to 105, one base test, race week at 0.50 of the peak week (the low athlete's shakeouts keep 38/25/20). trail_20k_basic_high 0.0043 -> 0.0000; trail_20k_basic_low 0.0160 -> 0.0194 (taper_volume_drop 0.04: the 12-week plan's taper and race week average 0.65 of a 2.9 h peak once race week keeps three shakeouts; race_day_freshness_ratio 0.01). 2026-10-07, the trail 20K rule review: basic plans deload every fourth week (3:1), the last recovery week sits three weeks before a two-week taper (R-PHASE-015) and no peak shed runs before one (R-PP-007); the hill session grows through the plan, the peak recovery long run is 55-70 min; rulebook 5 reads a one-week taper with its race week, grades the trail 20K's race week (0.25-0.50 [EX]), taper volume (0.40-0.60, the taper reviews) and taper quality (0.30-1.00, tr 11.3) on bands of its own, and covers it with first_long_session_fit and weekly_volume_ramp. A _high family (the default athlete at 1.5x) joins the matrix; the 8-week _wide cell went with the 12-week minimum. trail_20k_basic 0.0113 -> 0.0000, trail_20k_basic_low 0.0640 -> 0.0160 (first_long_session_fit 0.09: the low athlete's first long run is 1.18x their recent longest; taper_session_frequency 0.15: a 3-4 session week's taper counts one session more than its peak once the peak's progression run turns optional), trail_20k_basic_high 0.0043 (recovery_week_depth 0.065: a 4.6 h athlete's recovery weeks book the slot minimums, 1.9-2.2 h). 2026-10-06, trail 20K basic keeps its hill session in a squeezed taper week (the climb's share 0.45) and never books a steady or progression run under 30 minutes: trail_20k_basic_low 0.0951 -> 0.0640 and trail_20k_basic_wide 0.0707 -> 0.0397 (taper_quality_share 0.53 -> 0.00 and 0.55 -> 0.04, taper_session_frequency to 0.00; taper_volume_drop rose 0.05 -> 0.17 and 0.00 -> 0.27 because the climb card cannot go under 50 minutes), trail_20k_basic unchanged. 2026-10-05, the matrix grades the plans a menu offers (offered: in the menu YAML), so it holds the three trail_20k_basic cells and nothing else. They are first readings, held pending review. Off band: trail_20k_basic_wide, the 8-week plan (taper_quality_share 0.55, race_week_volume 0.20, taper_session_frequency 0.17), and trail_20k_basic_low, the default athlete at 0.75 of the recent volume (taper_quality_share 0.53, longest_long_session_in_peak 0.33, race_week_volume 0.20). The cells of the plans that are not on offer went with them and are read afresh when a plan returns; their last readings and their history are in git (b2cbdbfe).",
